<h1>Sign Certificate Signing Request</h1>

<div class="card">
  <form action="/csr/sign" method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data">
    <label>CSR File <input type="file" name="csr_file" accept=".csr,.pem,.req" required></label>

    <label>Sign with CA
      <select name="ca_id" required>
        <% @cas.each do |ca| %>
          <option value="<%= ca['id'] %>"><%= ca['alias'] %> (<%= ca['role'] %>)</option>
        <% end %>
      </select>
    </label>

    <label>Certificate Role
      <select name="role">
        <option value="intermediate">Intermediate CA (can sign other certs)</option>
        <option value="end-entity">End-Entity (signer — cannot sign other certs)</option>
      </select>
    </label>

    <fieldset class="scope-fieldset">
      <legend>Authorized Recommendations (scope)</legend>
      <p class="hint">Which OIML Recommendations can this cert issue CNMLs for?
        For intermediate certs this is the BIML-granted scope. For end-entity
        certs, scope must be a subset of the issuing CA's scope.</p>
      <div class="scope-grid">
        <% if @recommendations&.any? %>
          <% @recommendations.each do |r| %>
            <label class="scope-option">
              <input type="checkbox" name="scope[]" value="<%= r['id'] %>">
              <span class="scope-id"><%= r['id'] %></span>
              <span class="scope-title"><%= r['shortTitle'] %></span>
              <span class="scope-cat"><%= r['category'] %></span>
            </label>
          <% end %>
        <% else %>
          <p class="hint">Could not load Recommendation list from
            <code>packages/cnml-schemas/src/schemas/</code>. Run from the
            monorepo root.</p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <label>Validity (years) <input type="number" name="validity" value="2" min="1" max="25"></label>

    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Sign Certificate</button>
  </form>
</div>

<p class="hint">The CSR's public key will be certified by the selected CA. The CSR's
private key is NOT needed — only the public key travels in the CSR. Scope is
embedded as a non-critical X.509 v3 extension (OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.99999.1.1)
and also written to <code>trust-anchors.json</code>.</p>
